    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Divya Agarwal",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105191450404257160577/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVgOjU9F-dd4su-_ROGgpcKE95fo0cYtknXIWq1hswV6qm9IiaULw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "Cute little public park and event place where something keeps happening for the month of July- August. Love the fact that it is beside waters and have many activities to do, you could rent out games and also install a hammock and sit by yourself. There are few food trucks and drinks and snack bars where you can grab something or bring your own and sit and enjoy the place and vibe.",
        "time": 1723379144,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Stephan Rohan",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109380633517492525016/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVfviltg8WCkOsze3KfXrLlQHSOCdvpbokvZElxYYRtJUsw306uGw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "2 years ago",
        "text": "Superbly lit small park. Always full of events for the community. A place to be for the locals. La grande tablee is a giant table within the 405 for huge food gatherings. Beware after rainy days though, it might be muddy and lots of mosquitoes await.",
        "time": 1691238389,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Jean-Marc Provencher",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107923672926173694482/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXExGYB_1rYRMm14xObJOLfVAuan0ryLjzheNySwBTId5woLIz9=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "Nice place in any season but specially during the luminart festival in winter. Art by local artists illuminated and accompanied by music. Some interactive exhibits. Depending on the time fires are lit and free hot chocolate is served and it's free!",
        "time": 1738671633,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Gary Machado",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105547796614339530689/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUJWDp3MY_RJR520emno9rE8LdSLNEIEhD245gjj0foMhUcKun2hQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "3 years ago",
        "text": "A great addition by the city of Vaudreuil-Dorion. Lots of green space, picnic tables, workstations for remote workers equipped with power and free WiFi. Natural shaded areas thanks to the mature trees. Lots of activities, shows, events during the summer nights. Parking is very limited at the site, however you can park at camous Cité-des-Jeunes.",
        "time": 1658790381,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Lemuel Miravalles",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116724260265533044531/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLZyD4y-Z5-EPHeF_ap5buMbrDUtDesmNKsrbgs4BQKHOAE7g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 4,
        "relative_time_description": "3 years ago",
        "text": "Its our first visit in this place.\nThe place is beautiful, a nice place for small family outing, gathering or events.\nPeaceful. Relaxing.",
